## 📋 Spec Analysis

```
Feature name:     SmartQC — Test Case Generator Full Pipeline
Feature type:     Combined (Web UI + API/AI Backend + Claude Project Platform)
Actors:           QC Engineer, Tester, QA Manager

Main flows (Happy Paths):
  1. User uploads a valid .md spec → skill analyzes → generates test cases + report template
  2. User pastes spec text directly → same pipeline executes
  3. User specifies optional inputs (env, platform, coverage) → output scoped accordingly
  4. Generation cut off mid-run → skill stops cleanly → outputs resume instruction
  5. Sensitive data detected in spec → masked silently → notice prepended to output
  6. User resumes an interrupted generation using "Continue from TC-XXX-NNN"
  7. User requests rollback to previous version → skill restores previous output

Business rules:
  - Input must be a .md spec file (uploaded or pasted)
  - Skill auto-detects: feature type, platforms, main flows, edge cases, risk areas
  - Output always has 2 artifacts: test case document + report template
  - TC ID format: TC-[MODULE]-[NUM]
  - Priority auto-assigned: 🔴 Critical / 🟡 Major / 🟢 Minor per defined rules
  - Test Data must always have exact values — never "valid email" or "any password"
  - Version bump: patch (same spec re-run v1.0→v1.0.1), minor (updated spec v1.0→v1.1), major (rewrite v1.x→v2.0)
  - Security masking: 7 sensitive data categories, always masked before processing
  - Retry: max 3 attempts, 5s delay, fallback to partial output with resume flag
  - Language: match spec language; English for mixed-language specs
  - Apply all 5 test design techniques: EP, BVA, Decision Table, State Transition, Pairwise

Data entities involved:
  - Input: spec.md file (read)
  - Output: Test Case Document (created), Report Template (created), Version Log (created/updated)
  - Sensitive data patterns (detected, masked, never stored)

Dependencies:
  - Claude AI model (Sonnet) for generation
  - Claude Project platform for deployment
  - SKILL.md loaded in Project Instructions
  - User-provided spec file (quality directly impacts output quality)

Ambiguities:
  1. No explicit SLA for generation time — "2–5 minutes" is aspirational, not contractual
  2. "Roll back to v1.0" implies version files are persisted, but Claude Projects have no persistent
     storage across sessions — unclear how this works after session ends
  3. "GitHub push with each generation" (section 9) — no GitHub integration described in skill itself
  4. Retry mechanism (section 8) references 30s timeout — who enforces this? Claude API or skill wrapper?
  5. "Does not store conversation history beyond current session" conflicts with "roll back to v1.0"
  6. Max spec size / context window limit not specified — no guidance on very large specs (>10,000 words)

Risk areas:
  🔴 Security masking — if masking fails, PII/secrets leak into output (including obfuscated credentials)
  🔴 Incomplete output handling — if cutoff detection fails, half-written TCs go to QC
  🔴 Version rollback — depends on session persistence that may not exist in Claude Projects
  🟡 Spec quality dependency — vague input produces vague output with no clear error
  🟡 Multi-module specs — TC ID prefix assignment may collide or be ambiguous
  🟡 Language detection — mixed-language specs could produce inconsistent output
  🟡 Prompt injection via spec content — adversarial spec could attempt to hijack skill behavior
```

